WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
Hey explorers!

00:00:01.547 --> 00:00:03.087
Can two worlds help us draw?

00:00:04.427 --> 00:00:07.967
Mercury, the closest planet to the Sun,
goes around

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.907
in about 88 Earth days.

00:00:11.307 --> 00:00:13.327
Far away Pluto is a dwarf planet.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:17.587
One trip takes about 248 Earth years.

00:00:18.507 --> 00:00:23.107
One Pluto year is about as long as the
United States has existed.

00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:27.007
Mercury makes over a thousand trips, while
Pluto

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:27.847
makes one.

00:00:28.547 --> 00:00:31.627
Now, let's draw a line between them in our
simple

00:00:31.567 --> 00:00:32.047
model.

00:00:33.227 --> 00:00:35.067
Keep each line as they move.

00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:37.127
Watch the thread spread.

00:00:38.327 --> 00:00:39.947
Look at that beautiful pattern!

00:00:40.787 --> 00:00:43.607
These lines are our drawing, not strings
in space.

00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:45.407
What do you notice?
